1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
Car shakes

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,000
when you hit the gas?

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,200
That jolt is called a misfire —

4
00:00:05,200 --> 00:00:08,000
one cylinder skipping a beat.

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,300
A worn spark plug

6
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:13,000
or a tired ignition coil can point to it.

7
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,300
Steady check engine light:

8
00:00:15,300 --> 00:00:18,000
one clue, still fine to drive over.

9
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,300
Blinking? Stop —

10
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:24,000
that level of misfire can damage your catalytic converter.

11
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:26,300
Do not guess which part it is.

12
00:00:26,300 --> 00:00:29,000
We pull the code and check the coil —
free check, written quote before any work.

13
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Nick's Tire & Auto — Euclid Ave, Cleveland.
Stop by and we'll take a look.
